ance, and returning it."]],0,115],[7132940,20400,2,0.197,0.133,[[0,80]],[],0,116],[7158708,20406,15,0.597,0.431,[[0,81]],[["f88b05d3_5ac2fc92",27,0,1,"Disabled by default because the web client part isn't ready yet? I think we could enable it by default and disable it in the finch config later if needed. People will be able to try it more quickly…"]],0,117],[7169933,20412,71,3.042,2.433,[[0,82]],[["6da93b54_90e57fcf",28,-1,1,"give it a default value, in case someone forgets to set it"],["772b62ae_bcfd05ff",28,-1,0,"suggest defining GlicPinEvent just above this"],["b4f77fb4_688dae5d",28,-1,0,"I think you missed the metadata field here."],["d4bb23c6_7019d7bc",28,-1,0,"i'd like to understand how this will fit in, where will it be used? I don't see it being referenced even in the follow on cl. Can some of this be defined along with the PinnedTabManager?"]],0,118],[7173810,20412,96,3.042,2.433,[[0,83]],[["8e38926c_8ebe81de",28,-1,1,"Please fix this WARNING reported by ClangTidy: check: google-default-arguments default arguments on virtual or override method... check: google-default-arguments default arguments on virtual or…"],["1c14a81e_5985ed9d",28,0,1,"nit: ctors should appear before assignment operators."],["1e606fd0_e60899dd",1,0,1,"can this be = default;"],["3113d1b1_def7f946",1,0,1,"i think = default; here works"],["609ce545_5a51c341",1,0,1,"consider a constructor, GlicPinnedTabUsage has a lot of fields, and it might help a reader understand which fields should be set on construction."]],0,119],[7180180,20413,43,1.77,1.388,[[0,84]],[["d8a17aea_8203baaa",1,-1,1,"Doesn't this trigger need to be actually used in the event?"]],0,120],[7180204,20413,110,3.042,2.433,[[0,85]],[["471b36ae_759ef2f3",1,0,0,"IIUC this means that if we call PinTabs with a tab more than once, it won't notify again, and it will keep its original pinning information and trigger? I think that's the right behavior, but I just…"]],0,121],[7187426,20413,92,3.042,2.433,[[0,86]],[["f48beebb_abb64930",1,0,0,"This makes me wonder if we should change pinned tabs entries to be stored as a map keyed on `TabHandle`."]],0,122],[7189559,20414,41,1.77,1.388,[[0,87]],[],0,123],[7199187,20416,7,0.385,0.279,[[0,88]],[],0,124],[7201151,20426,44,1.77,1.388,[[0,89]],[["519874af_3d2e6a3e",14,-2,1,"nit: It's already pinned, so I guess the pin trigger here doesn't matter, but it does feel a little weird to pass unknown. I wonder if there's another option that would be easier to read."],["371f2a49_ac43a5da",27,0,1,"I think we probably need a special enum entry for new tab daisy chaining. It's kind of different from the other daisy chaining."],["6169495b_43a97c0d",27,0,1,"Add a comment explaining this. If the tab is already bound, then it already has a pin source and this pin source will do nothing. If it's not already bound, then this code path will ensure that it's…"],["cc376edc_6e956316",14,0,1,"Can't we use -> here?"]],0,125],[7226419,20427,96,3.042,2.433,[[5,0.583,2,55],[0,0.417,90,41]],[["33841df0_8b718722",29,-1,1,"this name is weird to me, maybe just kUnknown?"],["42502cb5_31bb5cd1",30,-1,1,"since we're mechanically copying the enum, I think we should assume the values match and just do { return trigger as PinTriggerMojo; }"],["6368b09b_5eb738ea",29,-1,1,"brief description of each would be nice, as it ends up in the public api"],["3bae7fec_26567cbf",31,0,0,"up to you but you could use the mojom enum directly in C++"]],0,126],[7249199,20433,111,3.042,2.433,[[5,0.568,3,62],[0,0.432,91,49]],[["a9c5210b_d651dcd2",29,0,0,"nit: i'd make this non-optional, same below. Otherwise there's two ways to sending the same information."]],0,127]]}